      "content": "the sleep disorder thing doesn't really fit though. with narcolepsy or whatever people are usually exhausted or have these sudden sleep attacks, but im the opposite. i feel more alert and \"tuned in\" than ever. it feels less like a disorder and more like an optimization. like my hardware is just running more efficiently than the standard version. do you think there's any theoretical framework for a subset of humans who are effectively 'overclocked' or naturally tuned to a higher cognitive frequency?",
